    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Niall Browne Estate Agents are delighted to present this detached three-bedroom bungalow at Ballynalty, a quiet rural setting in Glencorrib, close to Headford. Built in 1962, with a kitchen extension added in 2003, the house extends to approximately 102 sq m (1,101 sq ft) and stands well back from the road on a site of c. 0.12 hectares (0.30 acre), with a walled front garden, gated tarmac driveway and open countryside views.\r\n\r\nAll of the accommodation is on one level, off a long central hallway: a living/dining room to the front, an L-shaped fitted kitchen with dining area and back door, three double bedrooms, and a tiled bathroom with a walk-in, level-access shower. A separate store room, with a wash hand basin, sits off the hall — formerly used as a third bedroom/study, it is not currently considered a habitable room in the absence of an alternative means of escape, though it offers future potential as a study or pantry, subject to works. \r\n\r\nOutside, the driveway continues past the house to a gravelled rear yard with a detached garage/shed.\r\nThe house has been vacant for over two years and requires full refurbishment throughout, making it a genuine blank canvas for a buyer to renovate and upgrade entirely to their own taste. \r\n\r\nAs a pre-2008 home vacant for more than two years, it meets the property criteria for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, and eligible purchasers may qualify for a grant of up to €50,000, subject to Mayo County Council approval."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Detached 3-bed bungalow of c. 102 sq m \r\n Site of c. 0.12 ha (0.30 acre) 0\r\nA blank canvas for renovation\r\nStore room off the hall with wash hand basin (potential study/pantry, STPP)\r\nVacant 2+ years: up to €50,000 grant may apply*"
      },
